## Tool & Environment Quirks

- Use Read/Write/Edit tools for vault files
- Shell: bash (Git Bash/MSYS) — Unix syntax, forward slashes
- DOCX: open as ZIP, extract `word/comments.xml`
- Windows 260-char path limit: avoid deep zip extraction
- n8n CSVs: JSON-encoded columns — use PowerShell `Import-Csv | ConvertFrom-Json`
- PowerShell from bash: write to `/tmp/script.ps1`, run with `powershell -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File /tmp/script.ps1`
- **Large command output goes to a file, then tail/grep the summary:** `cmd > /tmp/out.log 2>&1; tail -20 /tmp/out.log`, then Grep the file for specifics; never pipe predictably big stdout into context.

