## State Management

**Priority: Live system > work files > memory > specs.** If conflict, ask.

- `Projects/[Name]/STATE.md` — status, last action, next step. Rewritten at checkpoints.
- `MEMORY.md` — stable facts only. No volatile project data.
- Fetch from source, don't memorize IDs/deadlines.

**Save STATE.md:** after milestones, before compaction, before session end.

Read STATE.md first at session start (it has status and next task); re-read it before starting the next task, and fetch volatile facts (IDs, deadlines, n8n state) from the live system rather than from memory.

## Compaction Instructions

When context fills: (1) Save STATE.md (2) Save work-in-progress to work/ (3) Continue working.

**Reload after compaction — don't run on the lossy summary.** After a compaction fires, re-read STATE.md + task_plan.md + the active work file from disk before continuing; the compaction summary is a pointer, not the source of truth. (Adopted 2026-06-15, [[2026-06-14-loop-stack-audit]].)
